Step 1: Check relevant components (check whether the integrated brake controller can send messages normally and if there are any faults);
           or connectors (loose), wiring harnesses (open circuit, missed power supply, blown fuse, terminal resistor, on-site EMC);
           Or CAN line (whether CANH is short-circuited with CANL; Whether CANH is short-circuited to ground; Whether CANL is short-circuited to the power supply);
           or other (check for condensation inside the controller);
Step 2: Let it sit for 30 seconds, use the diagnostic device to 0x14 and clear the fault. After clearing, run again for a period to check if the fault exists;
Step 3: If the fault still exists, power it back on and off again to check if the fault has been cleared;
Step 4: If the fault persists, after-sales service will use professional instruments to troubleshoot or replace the controller;

