Step 1: Check relevant components (check if XXX can send messages normally, check for faults);

Or connectors (loose), wiring harnesses (open circuit, power disconnected, fuse blown, terminating resistor, field EMC);

Or CAN line (whether CANH and CANL are short-circuited; whether CANH is short-circuited to ground; whether CANL is short-circuited to power);

Or others (check for condensation inside the controller);

Step 2: Let stand for 30 seconds, use a diagnostic tool to clear fault 0x14, then restart for a period of time to check if the fault persists;

Step 3: If the fault still exists, power cycle the controller and check if the fault is cleared;

Step 4: If the fault still exists, after-sales service should use professional instruments to troubleshoot the fault or replace the controller;

